  "query_preview": "..\nLatest satellite and radar data show mostly cloudy skies with\nisolated showers across the region. increasing convection is seen\neast of the coastal waters and will approach the islands during the\nevening, ushering in increased showers and thunderstorms later this\nevening, near midnight. Overall, an unsettled pattern looks to\ncontinue across the Marianas through the next several days, with \nthe islands seeing mostly POPs (Probability of Precipitation) in the\n30 to 50 percent range through the week. Tinian and Saipan will see\nsome brief periods of 20 percent POPs early in the week. Meanwhile, \nGuam and Rota will see periods of locally heavy showers Tuesday \ninto Tuesday night as a weak disturbance drifts by south of Guam.",
